{"skill":{"slug":"email-daily-summary","displayName":"Automatically logs into email accounts (Gmail, Outlook, QQ Mail, etc.) and generates daily email summaries. Use when the user wants to get a summary of their emails, check important messages, or create daily email digests."},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770277453029,"changelog":"- Initial public release.\n- Provides automatic login to multiple email providers (Gmail, Outlook, QQ Mail, 163, etc.) and generates daily email summaries.\n- Includes browser automation examples for both logged-in and manual login modes.\n- Offers sample Bash and Python scripts for summary extraction and reporting.\n- Features guidance for scheduled execution via crontab or launchd.\n- Lists security best practices and troubleshooting tips.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8230,"sha256":"6f357d254c3d1a672961b3f26ccc6584b7c85bf6d3c79ced335543cf6f22b53c","contentType":"text/plain"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033722313,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2d699a9eb4608712c643fab76316bbe64efea2ea17c156046b4f4366f616c9ce","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2d699a9eb4608712c643fab76316bbe64efea2ea17c156046b4f4366f616c9ce","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: email-daily-summary\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its reliance on highly privileged browser automation capabilities and potential for data exposure. It uses `browser-use` with `--browser real`, granting access to the user's actual, logged-in browser session, allowing it to read full HTML content of email inboxes (`browser.html`), take screenshots, and execute arbitrary JavaScript and Python code within the browser context. While the stated purpose is email summarization, the broad permissions and methods, including instructions for setting up persistence (crontab/launchd) and the use of `browser-use extract` which implies sending email content to an external AI service, introduce significant security risks that could be abused.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161416863},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":90,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":15,"checkedAt":1789033722313},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill’s email-summary purpose is coherent, but it handles private mailbox access in ways that need review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reusing a real logged-in browser session is useful for email summaries but exposes active mailbox sessions and locally generated artifacts; retention, redaction, and storage controls are not clearly specified.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The install step uses unpinned browser-use installation commands, so the installed automation code may differ over time from what was reviewed.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions give broad browser-use actions over authenticated email sessions, including eval, python, screenshot, and AI extraction; these are mostly purpose-aligned but under-scoped for sensitive mailbox content.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill documents cron and macOS launchd scheduled execution for daily summaries, including logs under /tmp, but does not provide clear opt-in safeguards, permissions guidance, or uninstall steps.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Reading email, extracting message details, and summarizing inboxes fit the stated purpose, but the skill also shows a password typed into a command line and saves mailbox screenshots, which are high-impact handling of private data without enough safeguards.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable granting browser automation access to your logged-in email. Avoid typing real passwords into shell commands, avoid saving inbox screenshots unless needed, store outputs in a private directory, and do not enable cron or launchd scheduling unless you understand how to disable it and protect the script and logs.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: The command-line password example is not necessary for the email-summary purpose and creates avoidable credential exposure.\n[SSD-3] expected: Processing mailbox content is inherent to summaries, but saved screenshots and extracted message details need stronger disclosure and retention controls.\n[RA2] expected: Scheduled daily execution matches the daily-summary use case, but persistent cron and launchd setup is high-impact and under-controlled.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Environment-variable credential guidance is only loosely connected to the browser-session workflow and is not explained as a supported secure secret flow.\n[T06] expected: The static persistence finding is supported by the cron and launchd examples; it is not malicious by itself but warrants Review due missing containment and removal guidance.\n[T08] expected: A third-party browser automation dependency is expected here, but the unpinned installation weakens supply-chain assurance.\n[T09] unexpected: The plaintext password-in-command example is artifact-backed and conflicts with safer login handling.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033722313}}}}}